\[
\text{Fe}_2\text{O}_3 + 3C \rightarrow 2\text{Fe} + 3\text{CO}
\]  
- **ZnO (Zinc oxide):** The ionization energy of Zn²⁺ is very high, making it highly stable.  
- ZnO reacts with carbon to form ZnO·CO (zardb.  
\[
\text{ZnO} + C \rightarrow \text{ZnO} \cdot \text{CO}
\]  
