A solution has a hydronium ion concentration \([H_3O^+]\) of \(10^{-4}\) M. What is the nature of this solution (acidic, basic, or neutral)?
</USER_REQUEST>

<GROUND_TRUTH>
To determine the nature of the solution, we calculate its pH using the given \([H_3O^+]\):
\[ \text{pH} = -\log [H_3O^+] = -\log (10^{-4}) = 4 \]

