Thus, $z = -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{6} - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}i$.

The conjugate of $z$ is:
$$\overline{z} = -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{6} + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}i$.

The point corresponding to the conjugate of $z$ in the complex plane is $\left(-\frac{\sqrt{3}}{6}, \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right)$.

