Thus, we have:
\[ \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} (\cos B + \sin B) = \sqrt{2\sin^2 B - 1} \]
\[ \frac{1}{2} (\cos B + \sin B)^2 = 2\sin^2 B - 1 \]
