\[ \frac{1}{2}bc\sin 45^\circ = 3 \]
\[ \frac{1}{2}bc\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\right) = 3 \]
\[ \frac{bc}{2\sqrt{2}} = 3 \]
\[ bc = 6\sqrt{2} \]
From the sine rule, we have $b = k\sin B$ and $c = k\sin C$, so:
\[ (k\sin B)(k\sin C) = 6\sqrt{2} \]
