\[
P(X = k) = \binom{n}{k} p^k (1 - p)^{n - k}
\]
In this case, \( n = 12 \) and \( p = 0.5 \), so the formula becomes:
\[
P(X = k) = \binom{12}{k} (0.5)^k (0.5)^{12 - k} = \binom{12}{k} (0.5)^{12}
