</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To calculate the average radiation dose to the living tissue, we need to convert the absorbed energy from Joules to Gray (Gy). The unit Gray is defined as the energy absorbed per kilogram of material.

1 Gy = 1 J/kg

Given:
Mass of liver tissue (m) = 1.6 kg
Absorbed energy (E) = 0.12 J

Dose (D) = Energy absorbed (E) / Mass of tissue (m)

Dose (D) = 0.12 J / 1.6 kg
Dose (D) = 0.075 Gy

So, the average radiation dose to the liver is 0.075 Gy.
