\]

The square of the four-momentum transfer is:

\[
Q^2 = (P_f - P_i) \cdot (P_f - P_i) = (P_f - P_i)_0 (P_f - P_1)_0 - (P_f - P_i)_x^2 - (P_f - P_i)_y^2 - (P_f - P_i)_z^2
\]

Substituting \( P_f = (E_f/c, \mathbf{p}_f ) \) and \( P_i = (E_i/c, \mathbf{p}_i ) \):

\[
Q = \left( \frac{E_f}{c}, \mathbf{p}_f \right) - \left( \frac{E_i}{c}, \mathbf{p}_i \right) = \left( \frac{E_f - E_i}{c}, \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right)
\]

Thus, the components of \( Q \) are:
\[
Q_0 = \frac{E_f - E_i}{c}
\]
\[
\mathbf{Q} = \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i
\]

