\text{Reaction time} = \frac{1}{1 - e^{-k \times 10}} \times 0.00785
\]

The reaction time depends on the rate constant \( k \). If \( k \) is very small, the exponential term \( e^{-kx} \) approaches 1, and the reaction time becomes very long. If \( k \) is very large, the exponential term approaches 0, and the reaction time becomes very small.

